meta {
  name: Create Rating
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{coreBaseUrl}}:8110/
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "shiftId": "shift-booked-1",
    "rateeId": "nursery-acorn",
    "score": 5,
    "comment": "Well organized, clear handover notes."
  }
}

docs {
  functions-core: CreateRating (port 8110). Sign in as staff-jane (the booked
  staff on shift-booked-1) first — rater/ratee must be the actual
  nursery/booked-staff pair on the referenced shift (§3/§4).

  This creates the ratings/{id} doc, which is all this HTTP endpoint does.
  In a real deployment that write fires recomputeRating (an Eventarc
  trigger), which updates profiles/nursery-acorn.rating. Locally there is no
  live Eventarc dispatch for Go (§7), so that recompute will NOT happen just
  from calling this request — see README.md's testing-gap note for how
  trigger handlers like this one get exercised instead (hand-constructed
  event payload, direct unit test).
}
